/-!
# Left inverse of the degree-1242 row orbit table

Every product row is checked by the kernel, using a literal left coefficient
which is also checked against the supplied inverse table. Checked index coverage
then gives the identity for every coordinate. The stored row vectors are the
rows of the certificate matrix, so this proves inverse times matrix equals I.
The exported `checked` theorem discharges the inverse premise of
`row_span_of_checks` in `OrbitBases.Assembly`.

Source: `../source/README.md` and `../../source/README.md`; literal ATLAS
M24G1-f2r1242B0 matrices; James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111.
Generated arithmetic inputs: `../source/generate.py` (family `RowInverse`).
-/

